stateDiagram-v2
  IDLE --> TACTIC: start signal HIGH (raw read)
  TACTIC --> SEARCH: opening done
  SEARCH --> ATTACK: opponent inside TARGET_ENGAGE_MM
  ATTACK --> SEARCH: lost > ATTACK_TARGET_LOST_MS
  ATTACK --> BACKOFF: side ToF <= 20mm held 350ms
  BACKOFF --> SEARCH: after SIDE_BACKOFF_MS (100ms reverse)
  TACTIC --> BACKOFF: side ToF <= 20mm held 350ms
  SEARCH --> BACKOFF: side ToF <= 20mm held 350ms
  EVADE --> SEARCH: after escape
  SEARCH --> EVADE: line edge
  ATTACK --> EVADE: line edge
  BACKOFF --> EVADE: line edge
  TACTIC --> EVADE: line edge
  EVADE --> STOP
  BACKOFF --> STOP
  TACTIC --> STOP
  SEARCH --> STOP
  ATTACK --> STOP
  note right of SEARCH
    Nothing in front closer than
    TARGET_ENGAGE_MM: runs the DIP-selected
    pattern at SEARCH_SPEED_PCT, or arcs
    slowly onto a far sighting.
  end note
  note right of ATTACK
    One steering law (steerToward): speed
    ramps with distance, turn is scaled by
    speed, so a hard bearing at attack speed
    counter-rotates the inner wheel.
  end note
  note right of STOP
    Highest priority: checked before every
    other rule, on every loop. Terminal --
    only a power cycle leaves this state.
  end note
  note right of EVADE
    Second priority (line edge). Outranks
    BACKOFF, so the reverse can never back
    the robot over the border.
  end note
